cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use v_ase, please cite the exact software version.
title: "v_ase: A local 3D workspace for atomistic structures"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Giyeok
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1130-7668"
    affiliation: "The University of Sydney"
    email: "giyeok.lee@sydney.edu.au"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lgyEthan/v_ase"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/lgyEthan/v_ase/tree/symmetry"
url: "https://github.com/lgyEthan/v_ase"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.2.35a1+symmetry"
date-released: 2026-08-31
abstract: >-
  v_ase is an ASE-native local browser workspace for interactive atomistic
  structure editing, trajectories, volumetric fields, periodic-interface
  workflows, crystal-symmetry and phonon analysis, publication export, and
  revision-aware collaboration with external AI agents.
keywords:
  - atomic simulation environment
  - atomistic modelling
  - materials science
  - scientific visualization
  - human-AI collaboration
  - research software
